  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:notes "Followup sweep (2026-07-19) from AG21-QA-2 finding report (PR #580 @ bf96dc86). Finding status: STILL OPEN across all branches. Occurrence evidence: s18-s20 have both replay_persistence and replay_resume_worker as mod declarations in peer_transport/mod.rs (60, 60, 56 lines with 'replay' respectively). s21-s25 show partial progress: replay_persistence extracted (mod declaration removed from peer_transport/mod.rs), but replay_resume_worker remains locally defined in peer_transport/mod.rs, and crate root remote_replay.rs exists with persistence functions. This is incomplete: the worker that coordinates replay resumption (replay_resume_worker) should not be owned by the transport layer. Immediate dispatch recommendation: promote_to_branch = s25 (feature/pAG-s25-live-two-daemon-proof @ c245c2ea). Merge-forward fix will close lower-branch occurrences automatically." .

